BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:April
DTSTART:20250516T193000Z
DTEND:20250516T215500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T193000Z
UID:TZvNdBwp6v
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 134 mins (2h14m)\n\nAn obstetrician who secretly pro
 vides abortions and other family planning services to a remote village in 
 Eastern Georgia finds herself thrust into the harsh\, investigative spotli
 ght when she loses a newborn while on duty in the unflinching second film 
 from Dea Kulumbegashvili (Beginning).\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/apr
 il
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hanami
DTSTART:20250516T223000Z
DTEND:20250517T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T223000Z
UID:JnMi1IJW7G
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nWeaving between the natural and m
 agical\, Nana lives on a remote volcanic island from where everybody leave
 s. Left by her mother soon after birth\, she will spend her life trying to
  find the right answer to the lingering question in her mind and soul: Sho
 uld she stay or should she go?\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/hanami
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Starman
DTSTART:20250517T010000Z
DTEND:20250517T023500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T010000Z
UID:CuPKWRlpci
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nJet Propulsion Laboratory scienti
 st\, robotics engineer\, and best-selling science fiction author Gentry Le
 e\, who was on NASA’s Viking and Voyager teams\, discusses his experienc
 es and views on the possibility of extraterrestrial life. Director Robert 
 Stone and cast member Gentry Lee scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/festival/starman
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mongrels
DTSTART:20250517T033000Z
DTEND:20250517T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T033000Z
UID:n5yEQSAT3J
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nIn this triptych of stories\, a 
 Korean father and his two children move to the Canadian prairies to help a
  town deal with its feral dog population\, all while making a new life in 
 a strange land and navigating the grief of an absent mother. Director Jero
 me Yoo scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/mongrels
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Invention
DTSTART:20250517T193000Z
DTEND:20250517T205500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T193000Z
UID:rU6V6kVkBn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 72 mins (1h12m)\n\nCallie Hernandez (The Endless) co
 -writes and stars in this inventive\, autofictional indie that evokes the 
 tone of a Haruki Murakami detective story\, as a daughter investigates her
  estranged late father’s experimental health marketing schemes. Director
  Courtney Stephens scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i
 nvention
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Nature of Invisible Things
DTSTART:20250517T220000Z
DTEND:20250517T234000Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T220000Z
UID:TXrXvTbFX8
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nGloria and Sofia\, two 10-year-ol
 d girls\, meet during the summer holidays while spending the days in a hos
 pital. Gloria is accompanying her nurse mother and Sofia is visiting her g
 randmother with Alzheimer’s. Their playful and delicate bond will help t
 hem navigate the fragility of life. Director Rafaela Camelo scheduled to a
 ttend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-nature-of-invisible-things
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paying For It
DTSTART:20250518T010000Z
DTEND:20250518T023500Z
DTSTAMP:20250518T010000Z
UID:q1KgG3YWWw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nSook-Yin Lee (Shortbus) adapts he
 r own ex-boyfriend’s welcomingly tender\, autofictional graphic novel\, 
 centering on a Toronto-based cartoonist who begins hiring sex workers when
  he and his partner break up but decide to keep living together. Director 
 Sook-Yin Lee scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/paying-
 for-it
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monk in Pieces
DTSTART:20250518T040000Z
DTEND:20250518T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20250518T040000Z
UID:n12cSO37cD
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nAs avant-garde multihyphenate gen
 ius Meredith Monk approaches her final project\, the immersive “Indra’
 s Net\,” she and her greatest protégés and collaborators relive and re
 interpret her storied career’s most enduring works. Director Billy Sheba
 r scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/monk-in-pieces
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
